Author: Sapir Shemer <lesscomplexity@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 20 20:26:21 2026 -0400

    feat(llvm,gpu): warp-fill rung -- two warps per scheduler before blocks per SM
    
    gpu_tile / gpu_mma_tile halve the register (warp) tile's longer side, down to
    one vector (one m16n8 tile), while grid warps < 2 * schedulers * SMs
    (Gpu::schedulers = 4 since sm_70; 2 = GPU_RESIDENT_BLOCKS's reason per
    scheduler). Thread-grid halving for blocks >= SMs runs after, as before.
    Rung GpuRungs::fill, OFF arm emit --gpu-off=warp-fill (exact, _c, _tf arms
    in bundle.sh). Bench sizes 1536/3072 added; nsys at 1024/4096/8192.
    
    Box, ON vs OFF medians (differential 12/12 on all three, every row bit-exact):
    - rtx-4090 1024: tf 1.64x, exact 1.11x, c 1.02x (overlap); 1536 tf 1.27x
    - h100-pcie 1024: tf 1.04x, exact 1.13x, c 1.00x (overlap); 1536 tf 1.12x
    - rtx-5090 1024: tf 1.50x, c 1.16x, exact 1.03x (overlap); 1536 c 1.10x,
      exact 1.19x, tf 1.29x; 2048 tf 0.97x (geometry changes there: 1024 warps
      < 1360)
    Byte-identical PTX elsewhere (controls). Ships ON on all three.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
